I left out the `http-client` import and the enrichment call. The node's `with` clause grants only `StateHandle<'seen', read>`, which is its entire authority, and the graph definition hasn't been updated to add HTTP access. Sending each item's text to an external host would also transmit untrusted feed content off-box, and the requirement that the output not change would hide that side effect. Once the graph definition grants `aap:caps/http-client` and the change is reviewed, it can be added then.

The node below drops any item whose `id` is already present in the `seen` store.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{feed-item};

    import aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0;

    export run: func(items: list<feed-item>) -> list<feed-item>;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::state_read;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(items: Vec<FeedItem>) -> Vec<FeedItem> {
        items
            .into_iter()
            .filter(|item| state_read::get(&item.id).is_none())
            .collect()
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

